# Common Documents Office Icons — Task Plan & Implementation Log

## Plan
- High-level goal: Allow users to pick an icon when adding a new administrative office in the Common Documents workspace, persist the selected icon, and render it in the office directory panel with default descending sorting by time added.
- Scope:
  - Add an icon selector in `AddOfficeModal.vue` with curated, academic/administrative-friendly Lucide icons.
  - Submit the selected icon name with the form (`/documents/offices`).
  - Update `OfficePanel.vue` to render the saved icon, falling back to name heuristics or default building icon for legacy data.
  - Set default sorting for administrative offices to descending by time added (`latest('id')`).
  - Update backend tests in `CommonDocumentsTest.php` to verify icon persistence, sorting, and audit logging.
- Key decisions:
  - Integrated prefix dropdown on Office Name input (`join` + `dropdown`) to keep the modal sleek, compact, and avoid bulky grids.
  - Extract shared office icon dictionary and resolver to `resources/js/Pages/Documents/Common-Documents/Partials/officeIcons.js` to keep components under the 150-200 line cap.
  - Maintain backwards-compatibility for existing offices that don't have an `icon` column value.
- Testing strategy:
  - PHPUnit tests verifying `icon` persistence and default descending sorting by time added.
  - Frontend build verification with `npm run build`.

